  "limitations": [
    "The observation is a bounded read-only snapshot. It is not a live monitor and does not prove that no process started after the observation window.",
    "The audit established Git 2.55.0 exactly. It did not retain exact versions for every auxiliary shell, hash, or process-inspection utility, and this ledger does not invent them.",
    "Registry, common-Git-directory, worktree, branch, reference, and custody identifiers are public logical labels. They do not disclose filesystem paths or private storage locators.",
    "Status SHA-256 values bind observer-produced status captures. This public ledger does not disclose path rosters, so those leaf digests cannot be recomputed from this file alone.",
    "The publication-synthesis archive checkpoint is bound to its full commit, tree, and single parent. That exact identity does not establish that the archived content is current, correct, or accepted.",
    "Exact, evolved, and absent counts are established only for the eight declared selected-path corpora. No such classification was established for the remaining registries or paths.",
    "The comparison summary aggregates ten target-specific rows over eight selected-path corpora. The C12 numerical and C12 Orca corpora each appear once against the integration candidate and once against live remote main, so the summary total is not a count of distinct paths.",
    "Stable patch-ID equality ignores commit metadata and some diff distinctions. It is not exact commit identity, tree identity, semantic equivalence, proof of integration, or exact custody.",
    "Custody is recoverability evidence within each declared boundary. It is not correctness, authenticity, publication readiness, merge approval, or permission to remove a source registry.",
    "The c10-forensic registry had one promisor remote, a blob:none partial-clone filter, and six promisor pack markers. The zero-missing observed-head check is bounded to objects reachable from that head with lazy fetching disabled; it is not a global object-completeness claim.",
    "The isolated c10-forensic bundle replay is custody evidence for the exact advertised archive commit. It is separate from the live-registry observed-head check and does not establish completeness of every live ref, unreachable object, worktree byte, or ignored path.",
    "The three C12 commits described as unreachable are unreachable only from the observed live-ref scope and are each exact advertised objects in a public-receipt-bound complete-history bundle. Those pairs no longer create a registry-retention requirement; other unadjudicated refs, worktree bytes, ignored material, and semantic dispositions still do.",
    "The primary repository's common Git directory is excluded from this sibling ledger and has its own retirement ledger. Non-Git copies and directories without an independently identified common Git directory are also outside this record.",
    "The checker is a snapshot-integrity validator. A pass does not freshly inspect registries, replay bundles, contact hosted refs, or authorize cleanup; those actions require a new external observation.",
    "No active owner was observed during the bounded process inspection. That negative observation is not proof of abandonment and grants no deletion authority."
  ],
